
= RunPodFarm Scheduler =

#type:     node
#context:  top
#internal: runpodfarmscheduler
#icon:     TOP/scheduler

"""Schedules PDG work items on RunPod GPU Pods for distributed rendering and simulation."""

== Overview ==

This scheduler creates and manages a pool of RunPod GPU pods to execute PDG work
items. Work items are dispatched over plain HTTP to a small worker daemon on each
pod; PDG's own `mqserver` runs on a shared CPU "sync" pod and is reached over its
public ports, so work item results and attributes come back through the standard
PDG path. Files move by `rclone` over sftp to the same sync pod, which mounts the
shared network volume.

The scheduler supports:
* Automatic pod pool management with configurable min/max pods and slots per pod
* Autoscaling from the measured cook rate, and idle pods retired automatically
* Budget tracking with a per-cook cost limit and a hard kill at 120% of it
* Pod health monitoring, with a dead pod's work items requeued onto another pod
* A shared network volume for Houdini, project files and the run ledger
* Per-work-item output download back to the local paths the ROPs were aimed at

Before using the scheduler, you need:
* A RunPod account with an API key and a network volume
* A RunPod template built from `pod/Dockerfile` in this repository
* `~/.rpfarm/config.toml` and an SSH key pair, both written by `rpfarm setup`

== Setup ==

# Run `rpfarm setup`. It writes `~/.rpfarm/config.toml` (API key, user name,
  volume and template ids, GPU priority), generates `~/.rpfarm/id_ed25519`,
  downloads a private `rclone`, and symlinks `~/.rpfarm/src` at this checkout.
# Create the RunPod template and network volume, and install Houdini onto the
  volume under `/workspace/houdini/<version>`.
# Add a __RunPod Farm Scheduler__ to your TOP network and set it as the scheduler.
# Leave __API Key__, __Template ID__, __Network Volume ID__ and __GPU Priority__
  empty to use the values from `~/.rpfarm/config.toml`.

== Cooking ==

On cook the scheduler will:
* Bring up (or reuse) the shared CPU sync pod and start `mqserver` on it
* Upload PDG's job scripts to the network volume
* Create GPU pods and dispatch work items to their worker daemons over HTTP
* Download each work item's outputs as it succeeds
* Terminate every GPU pod of the cook when the cook ends

== Tips ==

* Use the __Status__ tab to watch pods, tasks and spend during a cook, and
  __Kill All Pods__ to terminate anything left behind by an interrupted session.

* If pods are not starting, check the API key, template id, and whether the GPU
  types in __GPU Priority__ are in stock in the datacenter.

* Enable __Verbose Logging__ for detailed output to the Houdini console.

* Per-task logs live on the volume under `/workspace/ledger/logs/<cook>/`, and
  the MQ log under `/workspace/ledger/logs/mq_<cook>.log`. __Sync Ledger__ pulls
  the ledger down to `~/.rpfarm/ledger`.

@parameters

== Farm == (runpodparam)

Global parameters describing the RunPod configuration. Every one of these may be
left empty to fall back to `~/.rpfarm/config.toml`.

API Key:
    #id: rpfarm_apikey

    Your RunPod API key. Generated from the RunPod web console under
    Settings > API Keys. Empty means `api_key` from `~/.rpfarm/config.toml`.

Project:
    #id: rpfarm_project

    Project folder on the network volume: `/workspace/projects/<user>/<project>`.
    Empty means the name of the `$JOB` directory.

GPU Priority:
    #id: rpfarm_gpulist

    Comma-separated RunPod GPU type names, most wanted first; the first one in
    stock is used. Example:
    `NVIDIA RTX A4500, NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090`. Empty means `gpu_priority` from
    `~/.rpfarm/config.toml`.

Template ID:
    #id: rpfarm_templateid

    The RunPod template defining the pod image. It must be built from
    `pod/Dockerfile` in this repository, which carries the worker daemon.

Network Volume ID:
    #id: rpfarm_networkvolumeid

    The RunPod network volume shared by every pod, mounted at `/workspace`. It
    holds Houdini, the project files and the ledger.

Datacenter:
    #id: rpfarm_datacenter

    RunPod datacenter region. The network volume only exists in one region and
    a pod can only mount a volume in its own, so this has to match it. Empty
    (the default) means `datacenter` from `~/.rpfarm/config.toml`, which
    `rpfarm setup` records from the volume's own region -- set this only to
    override that for one node.

    NOTE: this parameter used to ship defaulting to `EU-RO-1`. A scene saved
    back then keeps that literal value in the `.hip`, where it silently wins
    over a correctly migrated `datacenter` in `config.toml` -- pods are then
    created in a region that cannot mount the volume, every task fails with
    RunPod's own opaque error, and `rpfarm doctor` still reports everything
    fine because it only reads the config, never the scene. The scheduler
    compares the two at the start of every cook and refuses to run on a
    mismatch rather than burning pods on it. If that stops a cook, set this
    back to `(from config.toml)` -- the empty menu entry -- and save.

=== Scaling ===

Min Pods:
    #id: rpfarm_minpods

    Pods created at the start of the cook. They are kept while work is queued;
    once the queue is empty even these are retired when they go idle.

Max Pods:
    #id: rpfarm_maxpods

    Ceiling on the pod pool. The autoscaler never goes above it.

Slots Per Pod:
    #id: rpfarm_slots

    Work items one pod runs at the same time. Raise it for cheap items that do
    not saturate the GPU; leave it at 1 for renders.

Idle Timeout (s):
    #id: rpfarm_idletimeout

    A pod with nothing to do for this long is terminated. 0 disables it.

Sync Pod Idle (min):
    #id: rpfarm_syncidle

    The shared sync pod survives between cooks. When the next cook finds it
    unused for longer than this, it is terminated first. 0 keeps it forever.

=== Budget ===

Max Cost ($):
    #id: rpfarm_maxcost

    Cost limit in USD for this cook. At 80% the scheduler warns, at 100% it
    stops adding pods, and at 120% it terminates every pod and cancels the
    cook. 0 means no limit.

Min Balance ($):
    #id: rpfarm_minbalance

    A RunPod account balance below this only produces a warning at the start of
    the cook; the cook goes ahead either way. 0 disables the check.

=== Outputs ===

Download Outputs:
    #id: rpfarm_downloadoutputs

    When on, each work item's output files are pulled from the network volume
    back to the local paths they map to as soon as the item succeeds.

=== Paths ===

Local Shared Path:
    #id: pdg_workingdir

    Specifies the root path on your local machine that points to the directory where the job generates intermediate files and output.

Remote Shared Path:
    #id: rpfarm_remoteworkingdir

    When enabled, overrides the working directory on the pods. The default is
    this cook's project directory on the network volume,
    `/workspace/projects/<user>/<project>`.

